cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CORTET, please cite the paper below."
title: "CORTET: CORtical TETrahedral meshing"
abstract: >-
  An automated pipeline that turns an individual triangulated cortical surface into a
  solver-ready tetrahedral mesh without manual repair, certifying the worst element
  rather than the average. Part of Gen2020, a programme of work on the biomechanics of
  fetal cortical folding at King's College London.
keywords:
  - tetrahedral mesh generation
  - fetal brain
  - cortical folding
  - finite element method
  - mesh quality
  - dHCP
  - Gen2020
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Davoodshahsavari1992/-CORTET-CORtical-TETrahedral-meshing-"
